            <div xml:id="d166">

                <pb facs="0345" n="297" sameAs="frus:frus1877/pg297"/>

                <head>No. 166.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Peirce to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Honolulu, Hawaiian Islands</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1877-05-29"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi>
                            29, 1877</date>. (Received July 6.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 392.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Inclosed herewith is copy of a note from
                    Mr. Carter, the Hawaiian minister of foreign affairs, dated May 24, instant,
                    informing the legation that His Majesty’s chargé d’affaires in London had been
                    instructed to give notice to the British Government of the desire of this
                    government to terminate the fourth, fifth, and sixth articles of the treaty of
                    1852 between the two countries, and that said notice is now given, for the
                    purposes set forth in the seventeenth article of said treaty.</p>
                <p>Mr. Carter verbally informs me that this government is quite willing <pb
                        facs="0346" n="298" xml:id="pg298"/> to consent that the treaty referred to
                    shall remain intact, provided the British Government withdraws its demand for
                    the enjoyment of the same rights and privileges as those granted under the
                    reciprocity treaty between the United States and Hawaii. It will be observed
                    that the British commissioner, in making the demand in question, did not propose
                    to give any equivalent or compensation for the enjoyment of the rights
                    demanded.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed>HENRY A. PEIRCE.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d166-a1.xml" xpointer="d166-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
